.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-capture 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-capture \- Captured command output: navigate what `exec` already ran, without running it again
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten capture\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Captured command output: navigate what `exec` already ran, without running it again
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-capture\-show(1)
Print a capture\*(Aqs pointer, or the lines a selection asks for, with no second run
.TP
batten\-capture\-find(1)
Resolve a stored tool response by the key it carries, with no handle to look up first
.TP
batten\-capture\-list(1)
List this repository\*(Aqs captures as handles, in a fixed order
.TP
batten\-capture\-prune(1)
Remove this repository\*(Aqs captures — the one removal path; captures never expire on their own
.TP
batten\-capture\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
